.TH DIPIBIM 1 "2026-08-27" "dvbipitools" "dvbipitools Manual"
.SH NAME
dipibim \- convert between the plain TVA XML shape and its BiM binary encoding
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dipibim
.B \-f
.I xml
[\fB\-i\fR \fI<path>\fR] [\fB\-o\fR \fI<path>\fR] [\fIoptions\fR]
.br
.B dipibim
.B \-f
.I bim
[\fB\-i\fR \fI<path>\fR] [\fB\-o\fR \fI<path>\fR] [\fIoptions\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B dipibim
converts between plain DVB-IPI EPG (TVA) XML, as produced by
.BR dipixmltv (1),
and its BiM binary encoding (ETSI TS 102 323, subclause 9.4). \fB\-f\fR
names the input format; the output is the other one. No mapping table:
.B dipibim
does not touch xmltv ids or URIs, it is a wire-format conversion only.
See
.BR dipibcg (1)
for distribution.
.PP
Each ProgramInformation, Schedule (with its own ScheduleEvents) and
ServiceInformation element is its own separately BiM-encoded fragment
(ETSI TS 102 822-3-2, subclause 4.3.1.1). On the BiM side,
.B dipibim
reads and writes TS 102 323 tables 56/57's DVBBiMAccessUnit shape: a
fragment count, then per fragment a length, a 16-bit DVBContextPath type
tag, and the fragment's own BiM bytes, wrapped as [4-byte big-endian
length][access unit][string repository]. No DVBSTP container, index
structures or versioning (TS 102 822-3-2, subclauses 4.5/4.6) are
produced or expected; see
.BR dipibcg (1)
for that layer.
.PP
Supported codecs (TS 102 323, subclause 9.4.3.3ff) are dvbStringCodec,
dvbLocatorCodec (string fallback only, optimized-branch locators
unsupported), dvbDateTimeCodec (full-precision 8-byte MJD+ms mode, always
UTC) and dvbControlledTermCodec (compact scheme+term branch only on an
exact table 69 match with an integer term). dvbDurationCodec is unused.
CRIDs are derived from start time at write time rather than stored; a
non-UTC source time round-trips to a different-looking CRID for the same
instant.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-input\ \fI<path>\fR
Input path, \fB\-\fR for stdin. Default: stdin.
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-output\ \fI<path>\fR
Output path, \fB\-\fR for stdout. Default: stdout.
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-format\ \fI<fmt>\fR
.IR xml | bim .
Names the input format; required.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
One line on stderr: channel/programme/fragment counts, plus output byte
size when encoding to BiM.
.TP
.B \-\-color \fI<when>\fR
.IR auto | always | never .
Default: \fBauto\fR.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show usage and exit.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B dipibim \-f xml \-i guide.tva.xml \-o guide.bim
Encode a plain TVA XML guide to its BiM binary form.
.TP
.B dipibim \-f bim \-i guide.bim \-o guide.tva.xml
Decode a BiM-encoded guide back to plain TVA XML.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B 0
on success.
A non-zero status is returned on argument errors or I/O failure.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR dipixmltv (1),
.BR dipibcg (1)
.PP
